Title: MUTUALS
Credit: Demo video
Author: Team Mutuals
Source: Facebook Closer Together AI Hackathon
Draft date: November 12, 2026
Contact: docs/VIDEO.md

/*
  THIS SCREENPLAY IS THE VIDEO.
  Edit it, then run:  node scripts/video/make.mjs   (re-captures the app, re-renders every frame, re-renders the PDF)

  Scene headings pick the kind of shot:
    INT./EXT. <a real place> - <time>        live action. A storyboard frame until we film it.
    INT. PHONE SCREEN - <screen>             the real app on the phone.
    INT. FEATURE - <name>                    the app keeps running, but no phone: the pieces that "pop out" sit
                                             big on screen, side by side, under the SUPER.
    INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - <name>            type, numbers and bubbles. No phone.

  Dialogue:
    NARRATOR (V.O.)                          narration. No audio and no captions in the video (we record the real
                                             voiceover later); each line still sets how long its shot holds.
    JAMIE / RILEY / anyone                   in live action: the line, shown in the storyboard frame.
    JAMIE  + (typing)  in a PHONE SCREEN     Jamie types the line in the message box beside the phone; when it's
                                             sent it flies into the chat. Muse's reply is real.

  Action lines in PHONE SCREEN and FEATURE scenes. The quoted thing after these words happens, in order:
    opens "..."        a Group by name, "the full shortlist", "the listing", or a path like "/digest"
    taps "..."         the button or link with that text
    scrolls to "..."   brings that text into view
    "..." pops out     the card around that text lifts out of the phone (or, in a FEATURE scene, joins the row)
    zooms in on "..."  the camera pushes in on the block around that text
    uploads "..."      a video from scripts/video/assets/ into Muse's video step
    waits for "..."    holds until that text appears
  Other words are just for us. They don't do anything.

  On-screen text (any scene):  SUPER: big statement   CAPTION: smaller line under it.
  Words wrapped in ~tildes~ get the Muse gradient.

  Notes in [[double brackets]]:
    [[steps Tell | Match | Meet]]   the "How it works" stepper; [[step 2]] lights up step 2
    [[network]]                     the Muse network: Jamie's Muse and everyone it's talking to, live
    [[phone away]]                  the phone slides out (also: [[phone left]], [[phone center]])
    [[zoom out]]                    the camera pulls back after a zoom
    [[stat 23% | text | source]]    a big number that counts up, with a bubble chart
    [[bubbles a | b | c]]           chat bubbles float in all over the screen
    [[secrets a | b | c]]           bubbles that blur behind a lock
    [[logo]]                        the Mutuals mark
    [[models]]                      the three Muse model cards
    [[activities 🛋️ Buy a couch / Marketplace | ...]]   cards in a row: emoji, label, and a small line after " / "
    [[post text | Group | footer]]  a Facebook post by our persona; ~words~ in the text get highlighted one by one
    [[agents]]                      our persona's Muse reaching everyone; most fall away, a few fit
    [[chapter 01 | Title | line]]   a chapter card
    [[funcard]]                     the fun-fact card Muse makes from the persona's profile (seed/users.json)
    [[reach a | b | c | d]]         rings around our persona, one per place Muse looks, people appearing on them
    [[hold 1.5]]                    let the current narration line finish, then hold 1.5 seconds more
    [[voice NAME: Voice]]           macOS voice used to time a character's lines (say -v '?' lists them)
    [[rate NAME: 215]]              how fast that character talks (words per minute), for timing

  Transitions: CUT TO: (a quick soft cut)  DISSOLVE TO:  SMASH CUT TO:  MATCH CUT TO:  BUBBLE WIPE TO:  FADE OUT.
  Scene numbers (#4#) are optional. Sections (# ACT ONE) are just structure.

  Timing is script order: narration runs over whatever comes after it, and the next narration line waits for the
  one before. Put a scene's SUPER and narration ahead of the actions they should play over.
*/

[[voice NARRATOR: Samantha]]
[[voice RILEY: Reed (English (US))]]
[[voice JAMIE: Eddy (English (US))]]
[[rate RILEY: 215]]
[[rate JAMIE: 215]]
[[rate NARRATOR: 210]]

FADE IN:

# COLD OPEN

INT. JAMIE'S DORM ROOM, STANFORD - NIGHT #1#

Half-packed boxes. An offer letter on the laptop: SWE Intern, Chicago, starts June 15. JAMIE (20) is typing a post in a Facebook housing Group. RILEY (20) leans over.

RILEY
Posting your budget to three thousand strangers?

JAMIE
I don't know anyone there. And I have to sell all this.

RILEY
Just ask your Muse.

SMASH CUT TO:

# THE PROBLEM

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - WHY WE OPEN FACEBOOK #2#

SUPER: We still open Facebook to ~get things done~.

[[activities 🛋️ Buy a couch / Marketplace | 💡 Sell a lamp / Marketplace | 🏠 Find a roommate / Housing Groups]]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Young adults still open Facebook for practical things. A couch, a lamp, a roommate.

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - THE NUMBERS #3#

[[stat 23% | of 18 to 34 year olds use Marketplace every day. The most of any age group. | Capital One Shopping Research, Facebook Marketplace statistics]]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
A quarter of us use Marketplace every day. It's where people who have what you need are nearby.

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - THE MESSAGES #4#

SUPER: Then come the ~messages~.

[[bubbles is this still available? | is this still available? | would you take $40? | can you do Thursday? | still available?? | lowest you'd go? | seen 3 days ago | is this still available?]]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Is this still available, eleven times. Haggling. Pickup times.

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - THE POST #5#

SUPER: For people, it's ~worse~.

[[post Looking for a room near the West Loop this summer! ~Budget $1,100, can stretch to $1,300.~ ~I'm up at 5:30 every day.~ ~Allergic to cats.~ DM me! | Chicago Summer Interns 2027 | 3,120 members can see this]]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
For a roommate it's worse. Your budget, habits and dealbreakers, posted to three thousand strangers.

BUBBLE WIPE TO:

# MUTUALS

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - TITLE #6#

[[logo]]

CAPTION: Your Muse talks to their Muse. You only talk to people who fit.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
We already ask Muse everything. So we built Mutuals.

[[hold 0.3]]

SUPER: Your Muse has the ~first conversation~.

[[agents]]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Your Muse checks with their Muse first. You only talk to people who fit.

DISSOLVE TO:

# 01 BUYING AND SELLING

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - CHAPTER ONE #7#

[[chapter 01 | Buying and selling | Film it. Muse lists it and finds the buyers.]]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Buying and selling.

[[hold 0.5]]

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. PHONE SCREEN - STANFORD FREE & FOR SALE #8#

SUPER: Film it. Just ~say what's for sale~.

Jamie opens "Stanford Free & For Sale" and taps "Ask Muse privately".

JAMIE
(typing)
Moving out of my dorm before Chicago, I want to sell my camera, my desk lamp and my mini fridge

Jamie taps "Video", uploads "room.mp4", and taps "Catalog items".

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Muse Ember watches the video, listens, and writes down what Jamie said.

The camera zooms in on "What I heard".

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. FEATURE - WHAT YOU'RE SELLING #9#

SUPER: Spark names each one, ~down to the model~.

Jamie waits for "identified each item". "Canon PowerShot" pops out.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Spark names each one from its clearest frame, with a used price range.

"Also in your video" pops out. Jamie taps "on Marketplace". "Listed on Marketplace" pops out.

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. PHONE SCREEN - FINDING BUYERS #10#

SUPER: Then it finds the ~buyers~.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Once it's listed, Jamie's Muse checks with every Muse that's looking for one.

Jamie taps "Yes, check".

[[network]]
[[phone away]]

The Muses talk. Jamie waits for "You decide who to talk to".

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. FEATURE - THE BUYERS #11#

SUPER: Fifty identical DMs become ~one small detail~.

Jamie scrolls to "between the stated budget and asking price". "between the stated budget and asking price" pops out.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Three buyers fit. Each one is down to a single detail, like a price or where to meet.

Jamie scrolls to "Meet at Roble lobby". "Meet at Roble lobby" pops out.

DISSOLVE TO:

# 02 FINDING PEOPLE

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - CHAPTER TWO #12#

[[chapter 02 | Finding people | Roommates, friends, someone to go with.]]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Finding people.

[[hold 0.5]]

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - YOUR FUN FACTS #13#

SUPER: It starts with ~you~.

[[funcard]]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Opt in, and Muse turns your profile and posts into fun facts.

[[hold 0.4]]

SUPER: Then it looks for ~overlap~.

[[reach This Group | Followers | Nearby | Your school]]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Then it looks where you choose. A Group, followers, nearby, or school.

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. PHONE SCREEN - CHICAGO SUMMER INTERNS 2027 #14#

SUPER: Tell it what you'd ~never post~.

Jamie opens "Chicago Summer Interns 2027" and taps "Ask Muse privately".

NARRATOR (V.O.)
For a roommate, Jamie tells Muse what they'd never post.

JAMIE
(typing)
I got a summer internship in Chicago and need a room near the West Loop from June 15 to Aug 21

JAMIE
(typing)
I can do $1,100 a month, honestly up to $1,300 if I can walk to work, keep that private

JAMIE
(typing)
I'm up at 5:30 for the gym before work, I'm allergic to cats so that's a dealbreaker, no smoking. Never share anything about my visa status.

SUPER: Public. Match only. ~Never shared.~

The camera zooms in on "Budget ceiling".

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Match only checks fit. Never shared never leaves.

[[zoom out]]

CUT TO:

INT. PHONE SCREEN - THE MUSE NETWORK - CONTINUOUS #15#

SUPER: Your Muse has the ~awkward first conversation~.

Jamie taps "Yes, check".

[[network]]
[[phone away]]

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Jamie's Muse talks to every Muse in the Group at once, and keeps checking as people join.

The Muses talk. Jamie waits for "You decide who to talk to".

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. FEATURE - THE SHORTLIST #16#

SUPER: Only the people ~who fit~.

Jamie scrolls to "Why it fits". "Why it fits" pops out.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Nora fits. Diego has a cat, so the Muses stopped early.

Jamie scrolls to "Your Muse stopped early". "Your Muse stopped early" pops out.

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. FEATURE - MORE THAN A LEASE #17#

SUPER: Then a reason to ~meet~.

Jamie scrolls to "More than a lease". "More than a lease" pops out.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
They both run on Saturdays, and there's a run club this weekend.

Jamie taps "Go together", then taps "Going". "Lakefront Run Club" pops out.

[[hold 1.0]]

DISSOLVE TO:

# SATURDAY

EXT. LAKEFRONT TRAIL, CHICAGO - SATURDAY, 7 A.M. #18#

Sunrise over Lake Michigan. Jamie and Nora jog past Ohio Street Beach with the Lakefront Run Club.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
A room, and a running buddy.

DISSOLVE TO:

INT. MOTION GRAPHICS - END CARD #19#

SUPER: You might have zero mutuals on Facebook today.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
You might have zero mutuals on Facebook today.

[[hold 0.3]]

[[logo]]

CAPTION: Mutuals builds them for you.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Mutuals builds them for you.

[[hold 0.7]]

FADE OUT.
